    <main class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">HUMAN CONTROL LAYER</p>
      <h1>ACCOUNTABILITY REVIEW INBOX</h1>
      <p class="lead">One place to see what is due, what evidence is missing, where to review it and which gates must be completed before an outcome can be published.</p>

      <section class="review-panel review-help">
        <strong>Required order:</strong> select a due checkpoint, verify and lock the original decision terms, add evidence that states both what it establishes and what it does not establish, then publish a reviewed assessment. A due checkpoint is not a verdict.
      </section>

      <section class="review-toolbar review-panel" aria-label="Review controls">
        <label>Administrator token
          <input id="admin-token" type="password" autocomplete="off" reader field="Held in memory only; never stored by this page">
        </label>
        <div class="review-actions"><button id="refresh-inbox" class="btn" type="button">Refresh Inbox</button><button id="clear-token" class="btn alt" type="button">Clear Token</button></div>
      </section>

      <div class="review-layout section">
        <aside class="review-panel">
          <div class="member-head"><div><h2>Due checkpoints</h2><p class="muted">Highest-priority items appear first.</p></div><span id="due-count" class="label">0</span></div>
          <div id="review-queue" class="review-queue"><p class="review-empty">Loading due checkpoints…</p></div>
        </aside>

        <section class="review-panel" aria-live="polite">
          <div id="review-empty"><h2>Select a checkpoint</h2><p class="muted">The item will open with its source trail, missing evidence and exact review forms.</p></div>
          <div id="review-workspace" hidden>
            <p class="eyebrow" id="workspace-lane">ACCOUNTABILITY TWIN</p>
            <h2 id="workspace-title"></h2>
            <div id="workspace-status" class="review-status"></div>
            <p id="workspace-question" class="lead"></p>
            <div class="review-links">
              <a id="workspace-public" class="btn alt" href="index.html#accountability-hit-list" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Public Twin</a>
              <a id="workspace-source" class="btn alt" href="source-document-vault.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Original Source</a>
              <a id="workspace-evidence" class="btn alt" href="evidence-vault.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Evidence Route</a>
            </div>
            <div class="review-grid">
              <article><h3>What is due</h3><p id="workspace-due"></p></article>
              <article><h3>Current state</h3><p id="workspace-state"></p></article>
              <article><h3>Evidence boundary</h3><p id="workspace-boundary"></p></article>
            </div>

            <div class="review-steps section">
              <section class="review-step" id="terms-step">
                <h3>Lock the original terms</h3>
                <p class="muted">Use the primary decision, order, filing, contract, vote or official announcement. Do not infer the actor, authority or promised benefit.</p>
                <form id="terms-form" class="review-form">
                  <label>Responsible actor<input name="responsibleActor" required maxlength="300"></label>
                  <label>Authority basis<textarea name="authorityBasis" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Stated rationale<textarea name="statedRationale" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Claimed public benefit<textarea name="claimedPublicBenefit" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Measurable success criteria, one per line<textarea name="measurableSuccess" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Primary source URLs, one per line<textarea name="primarySourceUrls" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Reviewer name<input name="reviewedBy" required maxlength="180"></label>
                  <button class="btn" type="submit">Lock Primary Terms</button>
                  <p class="review-message" data-message="terms"></p>
                </form>
              </section>

              <section class="review-step" id="evidence-step">
                <h3>Add checkpoint evidence</h3>
                <p class="muted">Add primary and counter-evidence. Every item must explicitly state its limits.</p>
                <form id="evidence-form" class="review-form">
                  <label>Evidence class<select name="evidenceClass" required><option value="official_record">Official record</option><option value="court_record">Court record</option><option value="regulator_record">Regulator record</option><option value="corporate_filing">Corporate filing</option><option value="budget_contract">Budget or contract</option><option value="corroborated_reporting">Corroborated reporting</option><option value="counter_evidence">Counter-evidence</option><option value="right_of_reply">Right of reply</option></select></label>
                  <label>Evidence title<input name="title" required maxlength="500"></label>
                  <label>Source URL<input name="sourceUrl" type="url" required></label>
                  <label>Published date<input name="publishedAt" type="date"></label>
                  <label>What this establishes<textarea name="establishes" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>What this does not establish<textarea name="doesNotEstablish" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Local evidence route<input name="evidenceRoute" value="/evidence-vault.html"></label>
                  <label>Submitted by<input name="submittedBy" required maxlength="180"></label>
                  <button class="btn" type="submit">Accept Evidence</button>
                  <p class="review-message" data-message="evidence"></p>
                </form>
              </section>

              <section class="review-step" id="assessment-step">
                <h3>Draft or publish the outcome</h3>
                <p class="danger-note">Publishing is blocked until the original terms are locked and every selected evidence item is accepted for this checkpoint.</p>
                <form id="assessment-form" class="review-form">
                  <label>Overall finding<select name="overallFinding" required><option value="too-early">Too early</option><option value="insufficient-evidence">Insufficient evidence</option><option value="supported">Supported</option><option value="partially-supported">Partially supported</option><option value="not-supported">Not supported</option><option value="mixed">Mixed</option><option value="not-implemented">Not implemented</option></select></label>
                  <label>Implementation status<textarea name="implementationStatus" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Public benefit status<textarea name="publicBenefitStatus" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Money and beneficiary status<textarea name="moneyBeneficiaryStatus" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Affected groups status<textarea name="affectedGroupsStatus" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Confidence, 0–100<input name="confidence" type="number" min="0" max="100" value="50" required></label>
                  <label>Plain-language conclusion<textarea name="summary" required></textarea></label>
                  <label>Alternative explanations, one per line<textarea name="alternativeExplanations"></textarea></label>
                  <label>Falsifiers tested, one per line<textarea name="falsifiersTested"></textarea></label>
                  <fieldset><legend>Accepted evidence used</legend><div id="assessment-evidence" class="evidence-choice"><p class="muted">Add accepted evidence before drafting an assessment.</p></div></fieldset>
                  <label>Evidence route<input name="evidenceRoute" value="/evidence-vault.html"></label>
                  <label>Publication status<select name="publicationStatus"><option value="draft">Draft for editorial review</option><option value="published">Publish reviewed outcome</option></select></label>
                  <label>Named reviewer<input name="reviewedBy" maxlength="180"></label>
                  <button class="btn" type="submit">Save Assessment</button>
                  <p class="review-message" data-message="assessment"></p>
                </form>
              </section>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    <section id="figure-source-status" class="section wrap source-status-panel"><h2>Figures & Sources</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Figures on this page</span><h3>Checked: 25 June 2026</h3><p>Numbers on this page are public-record leads. Crime, migration, sexual-offence, payout, death, and crisis figures must be tied to named official, court, police, parliamentary, regulator, or reputable source records before they are presented as settled.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Evidence standard</span><h3>What counts as a usable figure?</h3><p>Official statistics, court records, ministry releases, police datasets, parliamentary material, regulator data, or clearly named public reports. Nationality, foreign-born status, asylum status, immigration status, charge, suspect, conviction, and victim categories must not be mixed.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Document trail</span><h3>Open the underlying record</h3><p>When the figure matters, follow the document link, source file, court record, official release, PDF, book, or video. The visible page should help readers reach the underlying evidence fast.</p></article></div></section><script type="application/json" id="compatibility-marker-vault" data-cleanup-marker="deep-cleanup">{"status":"compatibility-routes-preserved-with-clean-public-copy","checked":"2026-08-02","routes":["downloads/forum-posts.json","downloads/forum-posts.md","feed-center.html","share-center.html","launch-room.html","offer-center.html","source-document-vault.html","evidence-vault.html","black-file.html"]}</script></main>
